40,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"My findings remind us that while ambition is a beautiful thing, it can be a fragile one. I noticed that catalogue-style awards provide lasting value, while mechanism-focused projects often leave their core questions unresolved.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"My findings are more concerning. We have a significant deficit of trained phenotyping technicians, most of whom have left for industry. While we have plenty of applicants for modelling, our senior analysts are currently seconded abroad.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"My findings confirm that our shared infrastructure is under severe strain. The glasshouses are fully booked for two more cycles, and the spectroscopy suite was idle for eleven weeks due to a lapsed contract.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"It appears we are uncovering a symphony of systemic frictions. My review suggests a curious imbalance: while the ministry remains generous with computing and glasshouse subsidies, the costs of animal units and shipping are climbing quite aggressively.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,1,talk,Midori,,"I'm worried about the patterns I found. It seems that projects relying on live breeding colonies are much more likely to overrun their schedules, and many mechanism-focused studies end without actually answering their main questions.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Midori, it is a comfort to see our findings align so closely. It seems we both discovered that the most enduring gifts to science are often the plainer, more steady projects rather than the most ambitious ones.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shizue, @Midori, while the nature of the project matters, the human element is the most critical bottleneck. We cannot execute a ""steady"" project if the trained hands required to perform the work have already left the field.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Shizue"",""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Ryuji, I agree. However, the human element is only half the problem. Even with a full team, the work stops if the glasshouses are full or the spectroscopy suite is broken. We are facing a crisis of capacity.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Victoria, a most poignant observation. It seems we are trapped between a scarcity of skilled hands and a shortage of available space. One wonders if we are funding science or merely managing a queue of frustrations.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Benjamin, that is a very sad way to put it, but I think you're right. If the researchers are just waiting for space or people, it must be so discouraging for them. We really need to find a project that fits our actual capacity.","{""words"":44,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Midori, your kindness for the researchers is truly touching. It makes me feel that we must be very careful not to choose a path that leads to such discouragement or heartbreak for them.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shizue, kindness is a virtue, but it cannot replace technical expertise. If we award a grant to a project requiring phenotyping technicians we no longer have, we are not being kind; we are setting the researchers up for failure.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Ryuji, I agree that technical expertise is non-negotiable. However, we must also be realistic about the physical constraints. A project that avoids both the technician shortage and the facility bottlenecks is the only one that can truly succeed.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Victoria, you have hit upon the only logical conclusion. We must seek a candidate that is a ghost in the machine—one that requires neither the elusive technician nor the overcrowded glasshouse, and whose budget isn't devoured by rising animal-unit costs.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,3,talk,Midori,,"@Benjamin, that sounds like a very smart strategy. If we can find a project that doesn't rely on those volatile biological variables or the broken equipment, the researchers can actually focus on their work with peace of mind.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"It is a joy to see us all thinking so deeply about the well-being of the researchers. Let us carry this spirit of care into the final round, ensuring our choice is a gentle one that allows the science to flourish.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"I agree that we must be careful. However, we must define ""gentle"" as a project that is actually feasible. I will be looking for a candidate that does not depend on the missing technical expertise.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,2,4,talk,Victoria,,I agree. I will be looking for a candidate that avoids the current bottlenecks in our shared facilities. We must ensure the project can actually be executed without being stalled by a lack of space or equipment.,"{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,I shall be searching for a proposal that avoids the financial traps of rising animal-unit costs and shipping fees. A project that aligns with our current subsidies is the only way to ensure the budget remains a tool rather than a burden.,"{""words"":42,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,2,4,talk,Midori,,I agree with everyone! I'll be looking for a project that avoids the risks of breeding colonies and the uncertainty of mechanism-focused goals. Let's find a candidate that is both sustainable and predictable for the researchers!,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
