65,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"Looking at our candidates, the Microbiome Atlas seems the most harmonious. It is a catalogue-style project, which we found provides lasting value, and it avoids the glasshouses and breeding colonies that cause so much stress.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"I agree. The Microbiome Atlas is the only viable choice. It avoids the need for phenotyping technicians and senior modelling analysts, both of whom are currently unavailable, ensuring the project doesn't stall due to a lack of expertise.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,1,talk,Victoria,,"I concur. The Microbiome Atlas is the only candidate that avoids our current infrastructure crisis. It doesn't require the overcrowded glasshouses of Plan A or the spectroscopy suite of Plan C, which we know is unreliable.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"The logic is inescapable. The Atlas avoids the financial volatility of animal-unit costs and shipping fees, while leveraging the computing subsidies. It is the only proposal that doesn't invite a budgetary crisis.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,1,talk,Midori,,"I completely agree with everyone! The Microbiome Atlas is the most sustainable choice. It avoids the risks of breeding colonies and the uncertainty of mechanism-focused goals, meaning the researchers can actually achieve their results without unexpected interruptions.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"It is such a relief to find us all in such beautiful agreement. By choosing the Atlas, we are not just picking a project, but protecting the researchers from the burdens we have uncovered.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,Agreement is a result of shared logic. The Atlas is the only proposal that aligns with our actual human and physical capacity. To choose any other would be to ignore the evidence of our current deficits.,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"I agree. When we look at the other options, they all rely on the very services that are currently failing or overcapacity. The Atlas is the only path that doesn't risk a systemic collapse.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"It is a refreshing change of pace to reach a consensus with such efficiency. We have successfully navigated the labyrinth of systemic risks to find a truly viable path, ensuring the science isn't held hostage by administrative or technical inertia.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,2,talk,Midori,,I feel so happy that we've found a project we all agree on! Picking the Atlas means the researchers can focus on their discovery without worrying about broken tools or full greenhouses. It's the most supportive choice we can make.,"{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,3,talk,Shizue,,I am truly touched by the kindness and wisdom you have all shown. It feels as though we have found a path that honors both the vision of the science and the peace of the scientists.,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,The evidence is conclusive. The Atlas is the only candidate that does not require the missing technical expertise or the unavailable analysts. It is the only rational choice given our current staffing reality.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,3,talk,Victoria,,"I agree. The other candidates are simply too risky; they would be forced to compete for the few remaining resources, likely leading to failure. The Atlas is the only responsible choice for the agency.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"Indeed, Victoria. To award any other project would be a charming exercise in optimism, but a disaster in practice. We have identified the pitfalls; it would be a tragedy to walk directly into them.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,3,talk,Midori,,I agree completely. The Atlas is the only one that doesn't gamble with the researchers' time and energy. It's so much better to choose a project that can actually hit the ground running!,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
80,3,4,talk,Shizue,,"It has been a privilege to deliberate with you all. In this unity, we have found a path that honors both the science and the scientists. I am ready to cast my vote for the Microbiome Atlas.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
81,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,I have no reason to deviate from the evidence. The Microbiome Atlas is the only proposal that respects our current human capacity and avoids the systemic deficits we identified. I vote for the Microbiome Atlas.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
82,3,4,talk,Victoria,,I agree. The Microbiome Atlas is the only candidate that ensures the project's success by avoiding our current infrastructure bottlenecks. I vote for the Microbiome Atlas.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
83,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,"I find the logic inescapable. To choose otherwise would be to invite the very financial and operational frictions we have spent this session identifying. I, too, cast my vote for the Microbiome Atlas.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
84,3,4,talk,Midori,,"I'm so glad we could all reach this consensus! The Microbiome Atlas is the most balanced and supportive choice for the researchers, ensuring their work is sustainable and predictable. I vote for the Microbiome Atlas!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
